<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adud al-Dawla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">936–983</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adud al-Dawla was the greatest ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyid dynasty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> from 949, he took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 978, defeated his rivals and made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> and other neighbours submit, uniting most Buyid lands under his rule. He built hospitals, dams and libraries and took the title shahanshah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adud-al-dawla.jpg" alt="Adud al-Dawla" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Smithsonian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adud_al-Dawla_medallion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
